Here are ten sentences that end in the word "apple":

1. For breakfast this morning, I ate a crisp red apple.
2. My grandmother's famous pie recipe calls for one Granny Smith apple.
3. The teacher smiled when the student handed her a shiny apple.
4. Nothing tastes better on a hot summer day than a cold, juicy apple.
5. Isaac Newton supposedly discovered gravity after being hit by a falling apple.
6. At the farmers market, I bought a basket full of every variety of apple.
7. The horse gently took the treat from my hand—it was an apple.
8. Snow White fell into a deep sleep after biting the poisoned apple.
9. My dentist always reminds me that an apple a day keeps the doctor away, but I'd rather just eat an apple.
10. When choosing a healthy snack, you can't go wrong with a fresh apple. [end of text]


